      "body": "X18 checks deletion targets against shelf anchors, but not against intermediate links’ locations. Consider `<state>/quarantine` → `<state>/cache/link` → `<core>/logs/recovery`, holding an original. Step 2 permits recursive deletion of `cache`: it overlaps neither the lexical shelf nor its resolved target. That deletes the intermediate link. The first sweep preserves `logs` using its cached anchors; the second sweep reconstructs anchors through the now-dangling shelf, no longer protects `logs`, and deletes the original. An in-memory model of the prescribed checks reproduced this sequence. X20’s explicit symlink-entry guard does not cover recursive deletion of the link’s parent. This affects direct disposer calls and aliases introduced after the gate, both explicitly supported scenarios.",
